  "nodes": [
    {
      "name": "Sticky: Template Header",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -816,
        -816
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## [YCAT/TEMPLATE] Long-Form to Shorts\n\n**This is the master template.** Save As Copy -> rename -> activate per client.\n\n### Pre-flight before activation (per client)\n\nSearch/replace these tokens to client-specific values:\n- `client-slug` -> client's short identifier (e.g. `acme`)\n- `REPLACE_WITH_CLIENT_YOUTUBE_CHANNEL_ID` -> their YouTube channel UC... ID\n- `REPLACE_WITH_CLIENT_EMAIL` -> their email address\n\nThen assign client's own credentials to every node:\n- Gmail trigger / send: client's Gmail OAuth\n- YouTube node: client's YouTube OAuth\n- Google Sheets: client's (or YCAT's) tracking sheet credential\n- Klap API key (httpHeaderAuth): client's Klap subscription\n- Gemini API key (httpHeaderAuth): client's Gemini key\n\n---\n\n### Routing (single shared inbox)\n\n- Clients email `shorts@example.com` (forwarded to YCAT Gmail).\n- Gmail filter auto-labels by FROM: `from:client@example.com → label client:acme`.\n- Each workflow copy's Gmail Trigger polls ONLY that client's label.\n- Strangers' emails match no label → no workflow sees them. Safe.\n- Belt-and-suspenders: a `Verify Sender` IF inside the workflow rejects unexpected senders.\n\n### Credentials owned by YCAT (set in template, never swap):\n- 🟢 Google Sheets - tracking sheet logging\n- 🟢 Gmail (your account) - sends review emails (client-slug self-test mode)\n\n### Per-client (set when copying):\n- 🟡 Gmail Trigger credential = YCAT Gmail (`you@example.com`)\n- 🟡 Gmail Trigger label filter: replace `client-slug` with this client's slug\n- 🟡 Verify Sender: replace expected from-address with this client's email\n- 🟡 YouTube Trigger credential = client's YouTube OAuth\n- 🟡 YouTube channel ID for schedule branch\n- 🟡 Klap credential = client's (or keep your own for testing)\n- 🟡 Review email recipient (Gmail node \"sendTo\") = client's email\n\n### Changelog\n- 2026-05-25 (Block 4): Loops swap → Gmail send node (self-test). For productized client version, TEMPLATE workflow keeps Loops support.",
        "height": 600,
        "width": 1320,
        "color": 5
      }
    },
